-- Test for oversized public-key session key.
-- This malformed PGP message was generated from a throwaway RSA test key pair.
-- A one-off packet builder encrypted an EME-PKCS1-v1_5 payload whose session
-- key field is longer than PGP_MAX_KEY (32 bytes).
-- The embedded key material is only regression-test data and is not used by
-- any production code path.
-- The message contains two concatenated Public-Key Encrypted Session Key
-- packets using the any-key key_id sentinel (0000000000000000). The first
-- packet triggers PXE_PGP_CORRUPT_DATA through the public-key session-key
-- upper-bound check; the second packet is preserved from the original
-- reproducer shape and is not reached.
SELECT pgp_pub_decrypt_bytea(
'\'::bytea,
'\'::bytea);
ERROR:  Wrong key or corrupt data
CONTEXT:  referenced column: pgp_pub_decrypt_bytea
